WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Speaker 1: There's a right wing radio host named&nbsp;
Wayne Alan Root, and he actually used to come on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.000
the show a few years back. He would have these&nbsp;
interesting back and forth with David. But over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.800
the past year or so, he's been most famous for&nbsp;
being adamant in this idea that Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.480
should run for Speaker of the House if indeed&nbsp;
Republicans take control of Congress after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.760
2022 midterms. With the idea there being that&nbsp;
Donald Trump can be the one to torpedo Biden's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.560
legislative agenda. And perhaps be the ones who&nbsp;
oversee impeachment proceedings. If Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.760
decide to impeach Joe Biden for whatever reason&nbsp;
they decide to come up with. Keep in mind that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.200
in order to be the Speaker of the House, you don't&nbsp;
actually have to be a member of Congress. So it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:41.200
not like Trump would have to run for a House&nbsp;
seat. He could just be elected by the majority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.080
of the body. If Republicans take control and&nbsp;
while traditionally the Speaker of the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.320
is a member of Congress themselves, they don't&nbsp;
actually have to be. So a while ago, Root came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.240
up with this idea. He was interviewing Trump and&nbsp;
he was telling him all about it. And Trump said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.400
you know, that's really interesting. No one's ever&nbsp;
brought that to my attention before. I'll have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.360
consider it. And it seems like at this point,&nbsp;
Trump just doesn't want to do it either because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:09.040
it would be too much work or it's just not the&nbsp;
top job in government. So he just doesn't want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:15.440
to pay any mind to it. So this prompted Wayne Alan&nbsp;
Root to ask Donald Trump about whether that means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:21.040
Trump supports Kevin McCarthy to be House Speaker&nbsp;
if Republicans take control of Congress. And Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:26.560
didn't want to say that he necessarily supports&nbsp;
Kevin McCarthy. Let's take a look at this clip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.080
because it really is interesting and it&nbsp;
has to do with this narrative having to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.760
do with Republican infighting. You know, I.
